  "summary": "Browser-based tools now expose harmonized GWAS, QTL, GTEx, and cancer variant data for direct interactive querying.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread across these three resources is the packaging of harmonized, large-scale genomic data behind browser-accessible interfaces. COLSTATS integrates 1.65M harmonized GWAS and QTL summary statistics (hg38) in a Shiny platform that runs coloc.abf colocalization interactively. CaRinDB is a web database that combines cancer-associated missense mutations with functional predictions, allele frequencies, and residue interaction network parameters. The Age effect explorer provides code-free browsing of age- and sex-associated expression changes across 54 GTEx v10 tissues, using precomputed linear-model results. What is new is the emphasis on precomputed, directly queryable outputs: colocalization analyses, residue-level network parameters, and tissue-specific linear-model results. These resources address distinct scientific questions, from regulatory variant colocalization to cancer missense interpretation to tissue-specific aging, and do not share a benchmark or method. The shared element is infrastructural rather than methodological.",
